module examples.err_layout_order

# plans/M7.md item B, 03-hardware.md §2. The sibling of
# `err-layout-overlap`, and the reason the two are separate goldens: one
# condition in the checker (`offset < cursor`) covers two genuinely
# different violations, and the diagnostic must not claim the wrong one.
#
# Here `earlier` occupies 0x0..0x4 and `later` occupies 0x10..0x14. They
# share no byte at all — nothing overlaps. What is wrong is only the
# declaration *order*: 03 §2's rule is that a layout's fields are
# declared in ascending offset order, so the bytes a reader sees going
# down the page are the bytes the device sees going up the register
# file. Reporting this as an overlap would assert something a reader can
# check and find false, which is how a diagnostic loses its authority.

@layout(mmio, endian=little)
struct Regs:
    @offset(0x010) later: u32
    @offset(0x000) earlier: u32
